{"raw": {"https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/6acbdb5fce3bee6d3c2afb7f": {"title": "Admission Counselor/Assistant Director of Music Recruitment", "description": "LutherCollege-Admission Counselor/Assistant Director of Music Recruitment Admission Counselor/Assistant Director of Music Recruitment Luther College Admissions Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description Wage: $36,000 - $50,000 SUMMARY : The Admission Counselor / Assistant Director of Music Recruitment is responsible for recruiting, counseling, and managing relationships with prospective Luther College students interested in music.\u00a0 Serving as the primary Admissions contact for prospective music students, this position develops and implements a strategic music recruitment plan in collaboration with Music and Enrollment leaders. Responsibilities also include individual college counseling (for all prospective students), group presentations, proactive communication, participation in campus visit programs, and evaluation of music activities and marketing strategies, with recommendations to strengthen effectiveness and outcomes. They will be involved in the creation of music marketing materials, enrollment reporting, and broader relationship building with key constituents. The position also serves as a liaison between Admissions and the Music Department and coordinates key components of the music scholarship audition process.\u00a0 Extensive travel during the spring, summer, and fall recruitment seasons is required. ESSENTIAL DUTIES and RESPONSIBILITIES : Recruitment and Enrollment Manage and implement an annual recruitment plan for students who are interested in music. Build and maintain relationships with prospective students and their families, high school counselors, community-based organizations, and other key influencers. Plan and conduct school visits, attend college fairs and community events, and represent the college at other recruitment events. Many of these will have a focus around music however, some will not. Monitor performance indicators (i.e. # of auditions) and adjust recruitment strategies accordingly based on enrollment goals and market conditions. Communicate with students and families via email, text, phone, virtual meetings, and in-person interactions. Collaborate with Enrollment colleagues and campuswide partners around visitor schedules and student cases. Student and Family Engagement Conduct admissions conversations with individual students and families. Provide accurate and timely information regarding academic programs, student life, financial aid, scholarships, and the admissions process. Assess and respond to student needs and opportunities throughout the recruitment process, especially for those interested in music at Luther. Admissions Operations and Counseling Maintain accurate records regarding recruitment travel, admission and scholarships. Utilize the institution\u2019s CRM (Slate) for admissions processes, communication, and data analysis. Ensure student information for all Dorian participants is added to Slate and perform outreach. Events and Campus Visits Participate in the planning and execution of campus visit programs, off-campus student events, and other recruitment activities. Assist with campus visit coverage, including counselor chats and event presentations. Travel to represent Luther Music and host the Luther Music booth at set conventions (typically 7 \u2013 10 per calendar year). Organize recruitment travel for music related conferences and conventions. Strategic Projects and Campus Partnerships Serve as liaison to the Music department and Dorian-related programming. Execute music scholarship protocols, audition planning (in-person & virtual) and logistics for music auditions. This may include partnering with Visit Event staff and Faculty to schedule auditions. Maintain inventory and ordering for Luther Music items shared with prospective music students Manage webpage content for the prospective music student pages on Luther\u2019s site. In collaboration with Enrollment & Marketing leaders, update print materials with a music focus for distribution to prospective musicians. Lead or contribute to strategic projects supporting enrollment goals, student recruitment, and visitor engagement. Oversee mailing projects for the Music dept. posters and All-State letters. Perform other duties as assigned. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES : 1-2 student Ambassadors with a focus in music EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE and SKILLS : EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE and SKILLS: Education : Bachelor\u2019s degree in any major required. Knowledge of Music and Music Education is essential. Must have strong communication, teamwork, and organizational skills. Familiarity with liberal arts colleges and fluency in a second language are desirable. Experience : One year of relevant experience preferred. Experience in sales, marketing, communication, counseling, or education is a plus. Strong written, and verbal skills.\u00a0Must be enthusiastic, goal-oriented, self-motivated, team-oriented, and capable of representing Luther energetically and positively to prospective students and their parents. Experience working with Slate (or a similar CRM), Google Suite, and Microsoft is preferred. Candidates must have a valid driver's license and a driving record that will enable them to be insured through the college. Ability to cultivate and develop inclusive and equitable working relationships with students, faculty, staff, alumni, parents, and friends of the college PHYSICAL DEMANDS and WORK ENVIRONMENT: This position requires traveling on a regular basis throughout the year.\u00a0\u00a0Occasional overnight and weekend travel is required throughout the year.\u00a0 When in the office:\u00a0sedentary work.\u00a0 Sitting, standing, and walking in well-lighted and well-ventilated office involved Job ID 13260153076 | Posted on October 12, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"}, "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/6aaadf2fce3bee6d3c264446": {"title": "CFL Technician", "description": "LutherCollege-CFL Technician CFL Technician Luther College Other Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description SUMMARY The CFL Technician is a full-time position and offers technical support, collaborative planning with the Head CFL Technician, and quality customer service for all events in the Center for Faith and Life. Wage: $16.64 - $19.58 ESSENTIAL DUTIES and RESPONSIBILITIES Offer services to Center for Faith and Life users, campus event planners, and off- campus guests including all sound, lighting, and audio\u2013visual needs.\u00a0Determine users\u2019 technical needs and explain technical options available. Work with the Head CFL Technician to coordinate space needs, availability, and planning for upcoming events. Uphold a standard of excellence in technical support for the CFL. Provide general support for Programming & Outreach. Assist as necessary with building management for the Center for Faith and Life. SHARED DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES (All Technicians) Provide technical assistance and general support for all events in the CFL Main Hall and Recital Hall for conferences, campus-wide events, the Center Stage Series, Christmas at Luther, festivals, concerts, college ministry services, camps, conventions and other special projects for the academic year and summer conference season. Offer technical direction for events, including implementation of contracts and riders. Read and apply light and stage plots from touring companies. Act as contact for the technical end of productions. Assess and arbitrate production costs including the rental and billing of additional equipment and assistance. Set up truss, curtains, lighting and sound system, and other multimedia equipment as needed.\u00a0 Load in, set up, and load out guest sets and equipment. Responsible for all aspects of sound reinforcement and theatrical lighting including design, set up, operation, trouble shooting, repair, replacement and inventory. Record lectures, concerts, recitals, and worship services in the Center for Faith and as requested. Responsible for technical support and set up of College Ministry Sunday worship\u00a0and weekday chapel services. Assist with other Programming & Outreach duties when needed. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES Assist Head CFL Technician in directing and offering guidance to student technicians, student volunteers, and members of the Performing Arts Committee. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE and SKILLS Education Bachelor\u2019s or Associate's Degree preferred. Experience At least two years of experience working with audio systems and/or theatrical lighting, including design, set up, focusing and repair, and multimedia resources. Familiarity with a Yamaha DM7 soundboard and Dante networking is preferred. Skills Commitment to customer service. Skills in leadership, team building, and analytical problem solving. Strong organizational and verbal skills Ability to work independently and with a team Ability to cultivate and develop inclusive and equitable working relationships with students, staff, alumni, parents, and friends of the college PHYSICAL DEMANDS and WORK ENVIRONMENT Must be able to work at heights on ladders, catwalks, and a personnel lift. Must be able to handle heavy lifting. Must be willing to work long and irregular hours including nights and weekends. Must be able to climb stairs, no elevator on premises. Mostly indoor work. Air conditioned in summer and warm in winter. Job ID 13062577229 | Posted on September 17, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"}, "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/6aa865bdce3bee6d3c25ed1b": {"title": "Transfer Credit Coordinator", "description": "LutherCollege-Transfer Credit Coordinator Transfer Credit Coordinator Luther College Other Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description Description Salary: $33,500-$44,600 The\u00a0Transfer Credit\u00a0Coordinator\u00a0plays\u00a0a\u00a0crucial role\u00a0in\u00a0facilitating\u00a0the\u00a0transfer of\u00a0academic\u00a0credit of students from dual enrollment programs, community colleges, other four-year colleges and universities, and alternative credit sources to Luther College. The Transfer Credit Coordinator evaluates, processes, and posts academic credits from prior schools so students can apply them toward a new degree program.\u00a0Reporting to the Registrar and working closely with academic department and program heads, this position ensures accurate and timely recording of transfer credit decisions and supports students, advisors, and faculty in understanding transfer credit policies and procedures. This position is responsible for the maintenance of transfer course equivalency tables in the Colleague student information system as well as in other web-based applications and transfer credit pathways.\u00a0Transcript reading software will be utilized and maintained by this position to ensure consistency, integrity, and accuracy transfer crediting. The person holding this position documents the needs of transfer students and communicates trends to their supervisor and other stakeholders at the college for continuous improvement.\u00a0This role will also include involvement in Registrar\u2019s Office tasks, and participating in admissions and advising related activities and events in support of incoming students. Duties and Responsibilities Manage\u00a0Transfer Equivalencies: Conduct\u00a0assessment\u00a0of\u00a0transcripts,\u00a0course\u00a0descriptions,\u00a0and\u00a0syllabi\u00a0to\u00a0determine\u00a0transfer credit, contacting stakeholders for approval as needed, and entering into the student information system. Maintain\u00a0the\u00a0transfer course\u00a0equivalency\u00a0data base and\u00a0update\u00a0the\u00a0student\u00a0information system (Transferology, Colleague). Utilize\u00a0transcript\u00a0reading software\u00a0to\u00a0ensure consistency,\u00a0integrity,\u00a0and\u00a0accuracy\u00a0in transfer crediting. Research\u00a0and\u00a0review\u00a0programs\u00a0and\u00a0courses\u00a0from\u00a0other\u00a0academic institutions,\u00a0contacting appropriate stakeholders as needed. Make recommendations for the determination of course equivalencies to the Registrar. Participate in the development and maintenance of transfer pathways and articulation agreements\u00a0with\u00a0colleges with\u00a0representatives\u00a0of\u00a0the\u00a0Office of\u00a0Academic\u00a0Affairs. \u00a0Provide timely and accurate information in the development of articulation resources. Communicate with stakeholders: Act as a focal\u00a0point for questions from academic advisors, the Director of Advising and other stakeholders regarding credits that have the potential to transfer. Communicate\u00a0and\u00a0respond to\u00a0student\u00a0inquiries about\u00a0transfer\u00a0credit\u00a0evaluation\u00a0results and provide guidance on next steps. Refer\u00a0students\u00a0to\u00a0other\u00a0support offices\u00a0on\u00a0campus\u00a0as\u00a0needed. Provide\u00a0excellent\u00a0and\u00a0timely customer service pertaining to degree exploration, transfer credit and syllabi evaluation, and degree completion pathways or scenarios. Coordinate\u00a0with\u00a0Admissions\u00a0Office\u00a0staff\u00a0and\u00a0other\u00a0stakeholders\u00a0to\u00a0respond\u00a0quicklyto queries\u00a0regarding\u00a0course\u00a0evaluation\u00a0and\u00a0transfer\u00a0credits.Must\u00a0be\u00a0familiar\u00a0with\u00a0Luther College majors, minors, and concentrations as well as Core Curriculum (general education) requirements. Maintain\u00a0positive\u00a0collaborative\u00a0relationships\u00a0with\u00a0Academic Affairs,\u00a0Admissions, Advising,\u00a0faculty, the\u00a0Center\u00a0for\u00a0Global\u00a0Learning and\u00a0other\u00a0campus\u00a0stakeholders. Participate\u00a0in all aspects of the\u00a0duties and responsibilities\u00a0of the Office\u00a0of the Registrar. Perform other duties as assigned by the Registrar. Education,\u00a0Experience,\u00a0Skills, and\u00a0Work Environment: Bachelor's degree is required. Two\u00a0or\u00a0more\u00a0years\u00a0of\u00a0work\u00a0experience\u00a0in\u00a0higher\u00a0education preferred. Familiarity\u00a0with\u00a0academic policies\u00a0and\u00a0procedures\u00a0of\u00a0a\u00a0college or\u00a0university,\u00a0preferably\u00a0a liberal arts curriculum. Knowledge\u00a0of\u00a0FERPA\u00a0and\u00a0records\u00a0compliance\u00a0in\u00a0an\u00a0academic setting. Ability\u00a0to\u00a0work\u00a0effectively\u00a0with\u00a0a\u00a0wide\u00a0range\u00a0of\u00a0populations\u00a0representing\u00a0diverse backgrounds, cultures, life experiences, and abilities. Ability\u00a0to\u00a0cultivate and\u00a0develop\u00a0inclusive and\u00a0equitable\u00a0working relationships\u00a0with students, faculty, staff, parents, and representatives of other academic institutions. Excellent\u00a0interpersonal,\u00a0written, and\u00a0verbal\u00a0communication\u00a0skills\u00a0required\u00a0to\u00a0meet\u00a0with students, staff, faculty and parents. Strong\u00a0organizational\u00a0skills\u00a0with\u00a0exceptional\u00a0attention\u00a0to\u00a0detail\u00a0and\u00a0ability to\u00a0manage multiple priorities. Ability\u00a0to\u00a0work\u00a0effectively\u00a0as\u00a0part\u00a0of\u00a0a\u00a0team\u00a0in\u00a0a\u00a0service\u00a0environment\u00a0with\u00a0frequent interruptions (e-mail, chat, telephone, and walk-in traffic) and still meet deadlines. Ability to work independently and to make decisions based on general guidelines. Proficiency\u00a0using\u00a0Microsoft Office\u00a0programs,\u00a0Google\u00a0Suite,\u00a0and\u00a0competence\u00a0with\u00a0a variety\u00a0of\u00a0software\u00a0applications\u00a0including\u00a0CRMs,\u00a0databases,\u00a0form\u00a0management,\u00a0etc. Evidence of previous project management certification/experience, preferred. Knowledge of student information systems, preferred. Familiarity\u00a0with\u00a0international\u00a0educational\u00a0systems,\u00a0grading scales,\u00a0curricula,\u00a0and transcripts, preferred. Physical\u00a0Demands\u00a0and\u00a0Work\u00a0Environment: Work\u00a0is\u00a0often\u00a0performed in\u00a0an\u00a0office\u00a0environment\u00a0with\u00a0frequent\u00a0in-person interactions and requires the ability to operate standard office equipment. Involves sitting for long periods of time at desk/office. Position will require occasional evening and weekend activities to support student registration,\u00a0commencement\u00a0weekend\u00a0and/or\u00a0admissions\u00a0events\u00a0and\u00a0programming. Ability to lift 15 lbs (student records; table set up at events) Job ID 13044896881 | Posted on September 24, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"}, "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/6a9f30ffce3bee6d3c24d71b": {"title": "Administrative Assistant (English; Modern Languages and Cultures; Paideia; and Religion)", "description": "LutherCollege-Administrative Assistant (English; Modern Languages and Cultures; Paideia; and Religion) Administrative Assistant (English; Modern Languages and Cultures; Paideia; and Religion) Luther College Paideia Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description Job Title: Administrative Assistant (English; Modern Languages and Cultures; Paideia; and Religion) FLSA Status: Non-Exempt FTE: .83 (10 months) Wage: $14.01-$16.48 SUMMARY: The Paideia Program and the academic departments of English, MLC (Modern Languages and Cultures), and Religion require a highly motivated, detail-oriented Administrative Assistant with strong interpersonal and written communication skills for a full-time position during the academic year and one summer month ESSENTIAL DUTIES and RESPONSIBILITIES: Communication and coordination among faculty and students: Managing the Paideia Office and the Language Learning Center and all their contents and people Serving as the first point of contact for the Paideia Office and the Language Learning Center Hiring, training, and coordinating supervision of student workers, including the management of time cards Organization: Maintaining the organizational manual of events, tasks, deadlines, etc. Organizing academic events, including lectures and senior paper presentations Helping make travel and other arrangements for guest speakers Maintaining Paideia faculty program calendar and calendars for student worker Scheduling rooms in Main for meetings, tutoring sessions, quizzes/tests Maintaining and retrieving electronic records Ordering departmental supplies Managing financial paperwork (e.g., for honoraria and reimbursements for guest speakers, department budgets) Program reviews: Assisting with the collection and collation of materials for program reviews Publications: print and web Assisting with the publication of the Paideia Reader Assisting with maintenance of web pages Texts and Permissions Managing Paideia book orders and desk copies Managing copyright permissions for course packs SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: Coordinating supervision of student workers EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE and SKILLS: Education: Associates Degree required. Experience: 5 years applicable experience required. Ability to work independently and take the lead on designated projects Ability to learn and use various software, including Microsoft Office and Google Suite Ability to cultivate and develop inclusive and equitable working relationships with students, faculty, staff, alumni, parents, and friends of the college PHYSICAL DEMANDS and WORK ENVIRONMENT: Office environment with frequent faculty and student traffic Ability to multitask and prioritize in a busy office environment This position operates in a professional, collaborative office environment. The role requires efficient and extensive use of computers, telephones, and other office equipment. This role operates fully on-campus in Decorah, Iowa but occasional remote work days may be available as needed for personal reasons. Work requires exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or the ability to lift, carry, push or pull, or otherwise move objects with a limited amount of force. Job ID 12991727204 | Posted on September 10, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"}, "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/6a73a1f92c9a538f927f715a": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Biology (tenure-eligible)", "description": "LutherCollege-Assistant Professor of Biology (tenure-eligible) Assistant Professor of Biology (tenure-eligible) Luther College Biology Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF BIOLOGY (PHYSIOLOGY) \u2013 tenure eligible Luther College seeks an Assistant Professor of Biology, a physiologist whose professional experience in biology has prepared them to contribute to our commitment to academic excellence in teaching, research, and service\u00a0for a tenure-eligible position to begin Fall 2027. We seek candidates with ability and interest in teaching\u00a0physiology and anatomy for nursing majors, upper-level electives for biology majors, the introductory level molecules, cells, and genes course for biology majors, and an all-college interdisciplinary course at the first year or senior level in rotation with other department faculty. Topics for upper-division elective courses could include immunology, vertebrate physiology, endocrinology, developmental biology, etc. The teaching load is six course equivalents per year, with lectures counting as one course equivalent and labs as half a course equivalent. Applicants should hold a PhD; ABD will be considered at Instructor rank. Teaching experience is required.\u00a0The successful candidate will communicate knowledge of, and interest in, teaching at Luther College.\u00a0Candidates should demonstrate potential for excellence in college teaching and effectiveness in mentoring undergraduates.\u00a0The development of an exciting research program appropriate for the liberal arts setting that involves undergraduate students and seeks external research funding is expected. Teaching and research facilities include well-equipped labs, housing and surgical suite for lab animals, physiological data acquisition systems,\u00a0anatomy lab including human body donor dissection, electrophysiological equipment, human performance equipment, bioassay equipment (e.g., 96 well plate reader), qPCR, Nanopore sequencer, and a microscopy suite including electron, light, and fluorescence microscopes. Luther College is located in Northeast Iowa, a regional hub for outdoor recreation, two nationally recognized healthcare systems, top ranked schools, business, agriculture, specialty retail, dining and tourism.\u00a0Major Midwest metropolitan areas within a three-hour driving distance include Des Moines, IA; Minneapolis/St. Paul, MN; and Madison, WI.\u00a0We are an easy drive to La Crosse, WI, Cedar Falls/Waterloo, IA, and Rochester, MN, home of Mayo Clinic. At Luther College, inclusion and\u00a0belonging are central to our educational mission and values. We are committed to the institutional change required for visioning and realizing a more equitable and socially just college and society. Strong candidates will have experience and vision regarding teaching and mentorship of students of multiple and diverse backgrounds with attention to structural barriers that limit access to educational opportunities. With support from departmental colleagues and the Center for Excellence in Learning and Teaching, the successful candidate will participate in program development, student recruitment and advising. Departmental and college service, professional development activities that support teaching or research interests, and the pursuit of research that involves undergraduate students are all aspects of working at Luther College. Apply: For full consideration, applications should be received by September 21, 2026.\u00a0Apply for this position at https://www.luther.edu/offices/hr/careers .\u00a0Applicants\u2019 dossier should include: Cover letter describing\u00a0your\u00a0interest in the position at Luther College, as articulated in this position description, and summarizing your training and experience appropriate to the position. Curriculum vitae. Teaching statement addressing your approach to teaching physiology at both the introductory and advanced levels; your experience and vision for inclusion and belonging through your work and student engagement; and how your teaching contributes to a liberal arts education. Evidence of effective teaching (e.g., sample syllabi, student evaluations, other course materials) to the extent possible. Research statement, including your plans to develop a program at Luther College and your approach to mentoring students. Unofficial graduate and undergraduate transcripts. Contact information for three references (name, affiliation, email and phone).\u00a0References will only be contacted for those candidates under serious consideration and we will seek your permission before doing so. The current salary range for assistant professors with 0-5 years of experience is $53,100\u2013$58,900 (academic year salary); placement on scale is dependent on credentials and applicable experience. Additional opportunities are available (start-up funds, summer teaching, summer undergraduate research, grant funded research, etc.). Inquiries about the position may be directed to Eric Baack, Department Head, Dept of Biology, Luther College, 700 College Drive, Decorah, Iowa 52101; phone: 563-387-1087; email:\u00a0baacer01@luther.edu. Additional information about the college is available\u00a0at www.luther.edu . Questions regarding the application process should be directed to hr@luther.edu. Job ID 12729542417 | Posted on August 6, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"}, "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/6a69006c2c9a538f927e2c85": {"title": "Communications and Administrative Support Assistant", "description": "LutherCollege-Communications and Administrative Support Assistant Communications and Administrative Support Assistant Luther College Other Decorah, IA Not Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description The Part-Time Communications and Administrative Support Assistant provides administrative, communications, and logistical support for Luther College's grant-funded vocation integration initiative. This position coordinates meetings and workshops, communicates with project participants, tracks grant expenditures, supports digital storytelling efforts, and assists with project implementation. Wage: $15.00 This is a part-time position averaging 10 hours per week for approximately 30 weeks annually. This temporary position is funded through an external grant and is contingent upon continued grant funding. ESSENTIAL DUTIES and RESPONSIBILITIES : Coordinate logistics for workshops, meetings, and other grant-related events. Schedule monthly and quarterly meetings, individual consultations, and project activities. Communicate with faculty, staff, and project participants regarding updates, deadlines, and events. Support digital storytelling efforts by collecting, organizing, and sharing project highlights and participant experiences. Maintain project records, meeting notes, and related administrative documentation. Track grant expenditures, maintain budget records, and prepare documentation to support grant reporting and compliance. Assist with purchasing, reimbursements, and other administrative processes related to grant activities. Provide general administrative support to ensure successful implementation of grant activities. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: None. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE and SKILLS: Education: High school diploma or equivalent required; post-secondary coursework preferred. Experience: Previous administrative support, office coordination, marketing/communications, or customer service experience preferred. Strong organizational skills with attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency with Google Workspace and Microsoft Office; experience with Canva or Adobe Pro, social media, or other digital communication platforms preferred. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Ability to cultivate and develop inclusive and equitable working relationships with students, faculty, staff, alumni, parents, and friends of the college. PHYSICAL DEMANDS and WORK ENVIRONMENT: Work is primarily performed in an office environment with frequent computer use. Occasional lifting of materials up to 20 pounds and movement between campus locations for meetings or events may be required. Job ID 12653673249 | Posted on August 4, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"}, "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/6a5a8ffb38f0f828e2734fb2": {"title": "Campus Responder", "description": "LutherCollege-Campus Responder Campus Responder Luther College Campus Safety Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description Campus Responders (CR) provide for the safety of people and property on the Luther campus. They perform multiple tasks including patrol of building and grounds on foot and by vehicle to deter and detect unwanted activities, report writing and managing sub-program areas as assigned by the Campus Safety Director. CRs take calls that are generally related to activities that relate to campus access, behavioral health issues, prohibited substances, student wellness checks, transport requests, student disturbances, disorderly conduct, noise complaints, suspicious persons\u00a0or trespassing. CRs are focused on responding to calls related to quality-of-life concerns and low-level community conflicts that do not require intervention by a behavioral health or law enforcement professional. With a focus on long- term solutions and individual student growth, CRs have a visible and tangible desire to protect and promote a safe and healthy campus environment. CRs excel at fostering a sense of community and providing needed services for all who visit the Luther College campus. Good communication, problem solving and customer service skills are essential for this position. Pay Range : \u00a0$16.50 - $17.00 per hour. Shift : \u00a0This position will work primarily first or second shift but may work flexibly across all three shifts. In your cover letter, please identify your shift availability. PRIMARY JOB DUTIES The foundational goal of CRs is to support campus needs, and foster student learning by addressing low-level unwanted activities as student learning opportunities, assisting as they grow into adulthood. Essential community and student interaction duties and responsibilities are: Interacting with faculty, staff, students, and visitors in a professional and courteous manner Creating written and or electronic documentation of incidents and routine activities Following written directives and established procedures Working through problems with logic, critical thinking, and sound reasoning Maintaining order on campus Responding to a variety of routine and emergency calls for service including medical emergencies Working with personnel from other departments to meet the needs of the Luther community Enforcing campus parking and traffic regulations in a fair and impartial manner Maintaining crowd control at special events including athletic contests. Conducting investigations of criminal incidents and/or Code of Conduct violations Developing and/or delivering crime prevention and safety education materials Using cell phones / trunked cell phones for communication Securing and opening buildings per an established schedule Performing other duties as assigned. Providing for a sense of safety and well-being on campus Providing direction to student campus responder assistants FIRST RESPONDER SERVICES: Dependent on qualifications, the incumbent will work with the support and direction of more qualified staff as part of a team that is responsible for preparing for and providing first responder services to the campus community. Incumbent must be able to utilize electronic communication systems and have excellent written and verbal communication skills. Must be able to maintain at a state of readiness campus medical equipment and supplies as well as keep equipment and vehicle clean and response ready. Essential Duties and Responsibilities are: Respond to emergency and non-emergency calls, and make care decisions quickly based on experience and training level Identify scene safety issues, implement, adjust, and maintain scene safety as situations change Handle non-medical situations such as crowd control and protecting the valuables of a patient if necessary Maintain emergency supply cache which includes, but is not limited to, restocking supplies, testing AEDs Be able to remain calm and deliver quality services in pressured, stressful, situations. EMERGENCY MANAGEMENT: The incumbent should be organized and have the ability to plan ahead, and quickly \u201cconnect the dots\u201d in fast- moving external events. He or she can remain calm and be decisive under pressure. In an emergency situation, the incumbent effectively collaborates and coordinates with people from all levels of the campus community and local government. Emergency response may involve special demands such as unpredictable work schedules and assisting others. May serve as a part of the campus emergency management function or as a member of a Continuity of Operations (COOP) Team. Tasks associated with this function may include: Tracking and reporting on critical incidents Serving on teams and work groups reviewing or modifying incident management or continuity of operations plans Assisting in the rafting or updating guidance documents and procedures Preparing alerts and notifications for a variety of events and situations EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, and SKILLS: A high school diploma or GED is required; some college is preferred. An Emergency Medical Technician qualification is desired, but not required. Must have or be able to obtain first responder training and qualifications, such as CPR, First Aid and AED training. Must have or be willing to obtain Incident Management training. Preferred qualifications include past safety, asset protection and/or customer service experience and training. Prior experience in a college setting or working with college aged people is desired. Applicants must have a valid driver\u2019s license with a good driving record and must pass an extensive background check. Ability to cultivate and develop inclusive and equitable working relationships with students, faculty, staff, alumni, parents, and friends of the college. PHYSICAL DEMANDS/WORK ENVIRONMENT: The primary hours for this position will be during the overnight hours, which generally the shift will run from midnight to 8:00am. The 24 hour, 7 days per week nature of the campus safety program may require the incumbent to work a variety of other hours, when needed. Scheduled hours will include weekends and holidays. The position can be physically demanding and may require the following: The ability to stand for long periods of time in both indoor and outdoor settings The ability to perform extensive walking and climbing of stairs The ability to safely operate a motor vehicle May be required to perform moderate lifting, bending and climbing May be exposed to environmental hazards including, chemicals, bloodborne and airborne pathogens May be required to work in all types of weather conditions. Due to the overnight work schedule, the incumbent of this position has been determined to be eligible to participate in the Luther College Tuition Remission Program. Job ID 12564851725 | Posted on August 3, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Related Jobs No related jobs found. Check back later for new openings. Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"}, "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/6a0382c5b4b307daeda3d63e": {"title": "Lead Custodian", "description": "LutherCollege-Lead Custodian Lead Custodian Facilities Services Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description SUMMARY: Ensure campus spaces are safe and clean for students, employees, and guests. Positions available in academic and residential buildings to support student life, academic operations, and other events on\u00a0campus. Starting Wage: \u00a0$15.50 - $16.50 per hour ESSENTIAL\u00a0DUTIES\u00a0and\u00a0RESPONSIBILITIES: The custodial staff\u00a0maintains building appearance and\u00a0cleanliness in\u00a0all areas; lobbies, entrances, classrooms,\u00a0offices, hallways,\u00a0kitchens,\u00a0conference rooms,\u00a0staircases,\u00a0study\u00a0lounges; restrooms,\u00a0and shower rooms. Custodial\u00a0duties\u00a0will\u00a0consist\u00a0of\u00a0but\u00a0not\u00a0limited\u00a0to: Unlock/lock building\u00a0and\u00a0turn\u00a0on/off\u00a0lights Sweep Mop Vacuum Empty\u00a0trash\u00a0receptacles\u00a0and\u00a0dispose\u00a0of\u00a0trash Clean\u00a0glass Dust\u00a0surface areas Disinfect\u00a0fixtures Annual\u00a0deep\u00a0cleaning Assist\u00a0with\u00a0set-up for\u00a0campus\u00a0events Snow\u00a0removal Maintain\u00a0outside entrances\u00a0year\u00a0round Recycling Clean\u00a0restroom and\u00a0show-room\u00a0facilities Floor\u00a0care Other\u00a0duties as\u00a0assigned SUPERVISORY\u00a0RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide guidance\u00a0and\u00a0organization\u00a0to\u00a0other\u00a0team members Direct\u00a0and support\u00a0student workers EDUCATION,\u00a0EXPERIENCE\u00a0and\u00a0SKILLS: Education: High\u00a0School\u00a0diploma\u00a0and/or\u00a0equivalent\u00a0preferred\u00a0but\u00a0not\u00a0required Experience: 1 year direct experience in custodial work Must\u00a0be\u00a0detail orientated\u00a0and\u00a0have good\u00a0time\u00a0management\u00a0and\u00a0organizational\u00a0skills Basic\u00a0computer knowledge\u00a0and\u00a0operation Proven\u00a0ability\u00a0to work\u00a0with\u00a0others Must be\u00a0able\u00a0to\u00a0read\u00a0sufficiently to\u00a0follow instructions, ability to mix\u00a0appropriate chemical dilution ratio and understand directions for use Ability\u00a0to\u00a0cultivate and\u00a0develop\u00a0inclusive\u00a0and\u00a0equitable\u00a0working relationships\u00a0with students,\u00a0faculty, staff,\u00a0alumni, parents,\u00a0and friends\u00a0of the college PHYSICAL\u00a0DEMANDS and\u00a0WORK\u00a0ENVIRONMENT: Mobility:\u00a0walk\u00a0or\u00a0stand\u00a0for\u00a0extended periods\u00a0of\u00a0time Lifting:\u00a0ability\u00a0to\u00a0lift\u00a0and\u00a0carry\u00a050 pounds Dexterity: \u00a0must have\u00a0a\u00a0full\u00a0range\u00a0of\u00a0motion including\u00a0bending,\u00a0stretching,\u00a0lifting,\u00a0and\u00a0kneeling. Be\u00a0available\u00a0for\u00a0scheduled\u00a0shift Overtime\u00a0may\u00a0be\u00a0required Inside\u00a0and\u00a0outside\u00a0of\u00a0buildings,\u00a0spaces\u00a0may\u00a0or\u00a0may\u00a0not\u00a0be\u00a0air\u00a0conditioned Exposure\u00a0to\u00a0potentially hazardous\u00a0chemicals,\u00a0noise,\u00a0dust\u00a0and\u00a0fumes Required\u00a0to\u00a0work\u00a0in\u00a0restricted places\u00a0which\u00a0may\u00a0require stooping,\u00a0bending\u00a0and\u00a0kneeling Buildings\u00a0and\u00a0grounds are\u00a0smoke free Job ID 11994657718 | Posted on May 12, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Related Jobs Boiler Operator & Maintenance Technician Facilities Services Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible SUMMARY   Operate the Luther College Heating Plant in such a manner as to provide a constant uninterrupted supply of steam to the Luther campus. Maintain and validate automation systems for proper a Custodial Staff Facilities Services Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible SUMMARY:   Ensure campus spaces are safe and clean for students, employees, and guests. Positions available in academic and residential buildings to support student life, academic operations, and ot Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"}, "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/69d7b75daa7bfffa4b456380": {"title": "Boiler Operator & Maintenance Technician", "description": "LutherCollege-Boiler Operator & Maintenance Technician Boiler Operator & Maintenance Technician Facilities Services Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description SUMMARY Operate the Luther College Heating Plant in such a manner as to provide a constant uninterrupted supply of steam to the Luther campus. Maintain and validate automation systems for proper and accurate operation.\u00a0 Help to analyze data to determine operational savings. Perform this service at all times in a safe method to insure personal safety and safety to all Luther College faculty, staff, students and guests. Wage\u00a0Range: $17.34-$20.40 ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Operate boilers safely while being alert and able to handle emergencies. Perform proper water tests; boiler, softener, and condensate. Work safely with chemicals, steam, and 190+ --degree water. Maintain all plant daily records. Do required pool tests, record keeping, and filter maintenance, especially prior to pool opening. Test and maintain all steam lines to buildings. Test cooling towers for proper chemicals and operation. Record operational data for chillers and water softeners. Review Automated Logic building automation system for: Proper set points Verify operational parameters Check actual values to reported values Re-commission controls on a schedule Log operational data for further system cost review Perform preventative work or repairs from the work order system Plumbing Requests Mechanical/HVAC Requests Replacing lamps, shutting off circuits, resetting circuit breakers, etc Other requests that may come up Handle all types of work requests on weekends that come up Welding/brazing for college repair work Metal fabrication for needs on campus Assist in unloading fuel transports. Other work as assigned. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES May need to supervise student workers. QUALIFICATIONS To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.\u00a0 The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skills, and/or ability required.\u00a0 Must be able to read, follow and give direction.\u00a0 Must be able to diagnose problems and determine an appropriate solution.\u00a0 Must be able to read and interpret blueprints for troubleshooting. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE High School Diploma required. Mechanical or electrical background Experience with boiler operation Will need computer skills for spreadsheets, monitoring computerized building automation system, e-mail, etc. Ability to cultivate and develop inclusive and equitable working relationships with students, faculty, staff, alumni, parents, and friends of the college. CERTIFICATES, LICENSES, REGISTRATIONS Driver\u2019s License. Boiler Operator 1 (ability to obtain through Luther) Boiler Operator 2 (ability to obtain through Luther) Certified Pool Operator (CPO) (ability to obtain through Luther) Private School or College Routine Maintenance Specialty License (ability to obtain through Luther). PHYSICAL DEMANDS Mobility: ability to ascend and descend ladders of various heights, stairs, scaffolding and ramps; not be afraid of heights; walk or stand for extended periods of time. Lifting: ability to lift and hold 75 pounds, frequently lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects up to 50 pounds, lifting and holding 10-25 pounds above head. Dexterity: must have a full range of motion in the upper extremities; manual dexterity to operate equipment including scissors lifts, power tools and hand tools; ability to work for extended periods with arms above head. WORK ENVIRONMENT Inside and outside buildings---working in temperatures that range from heated rooms to outside temperatures of extreme heat and cold. High noise levels. Extreme temperature changes. Buildings and grounds are smoke/tobacco free. Shifts up to 12 hrs. Night shift possible. Overtime may be required. Will need to work rotating weekends and be on call. Some areas may be poorly ventilated or heavily congested. Exposure to potentially hazardous chemicals, noise, dust and fumes. Required to work in restricted places which may require stooping, bending and kneeling. Job ID 11710587411 | Posted on September 22, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"}, "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/69d7b5a5aa7bfffa4b4561b1": {"title": "Custodial Staff", "description": "LutherCollege-Custodial Staff Custodial Staff Facilities Services Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description SUMMARY: Ensure campus spaces are safe and clean for students, employees, and guests. Positions available in academic and residential buildings to support student life, academic operations, and other events on\u00a0campus. Starting Wage: \u00a0$14.00 - $15.00 per hour Full-time and part-time Positions Available Positions available in first, second, and third shift Shift differential pay +$.75/hour or +$1.50/hour Opportunities to advance to Custodial Lead +$1.50/hour ESSENTIAL\u00a0DUTIES\u00a0and\u00a0RESPONSIBILITIES: The custodial staff\u00a0maintains building appearance and\u00a0cleanliness in\u00a0all areas; lobbies, entrances, classrooms,\u00a0offices, hallways,\u00a0kitchens,\u00a0conference rooms,\u00a0staircases,\u00a0study\u00a0lounges; restrooms,\u00a0and shower rooms. Custodial\u00a0duties\u00a0will\u00a0consist\u00a0of\u00a0but\u00a0not\u00a0limited\u00a0to: Unlock/lock building\u00a0and\u00a0turn\u00a0on/off\u00a0lights Sweep Mop Vacuum Empty\u00a0trash\u00a0receptacles\u00a0and\u00a0dispose\u00a0of\u00a0trash Clean\u00a0glass Dust\u00a0surface areas Disinfect\u00a0fixtures Annual\u00a0deep\u00a0cleaning Assist\u00a0with\u00a0set-up for\u00a0campus\u00a0events Snow\u00a0removal Maintain\u00a0outside entrances\u00a0year\u00a0round Recycling Clean\u00a0restroom and\u00a0show-room\u00a0facilities Floor\u00a0care Other\u00a0duties as\u00a0assigned SUPERVISORY\u00a0RESPONSIBILITIES: If this\u00a0particular\u00a0position is a lead position,\u00a0you\u00a0will provide\u00a0guidance\u00a0and\u00a0organization\u00a0to\u00a0other\u00a0team members in your building You\u00a0may\u00a0be\u00a0asked\u00a0to\u00a0direct\u00a0student and\u00a0support\u00a0student workers EDUCATION,\u00a0EXPERIENCE\u00a0and\u00a0SKILLS: Education: High\u00a0School\u00a0diploma\u00a0and/or\u00a0equivalent\u00a0preferred\u00a0but\u00a0not\u00a0required Experience: Must\u00a0be\u00a0detail orientated\u00a0and\u00a0have good\u00a0time\u00a0management\u00a0and\u00a0organizational\u00a0skills. Basic\u00a0computer knowledge\u00a0and\u00a0operation Proven\u00a0ability\u00a0to work\u00a0with\u00a0others Must be\u00a0able\u00a0to\u00a0read\u00a0sufficiently to\u00a0follow instructions, ability to mix\u00a0appropriate chemical dilution ratio and understand directions for use. Ability\u00a0to\u00a0cultivate and\u00a0develop\u00a0inclusive\u00a0and\u00a0equitable\u00a0working relationships\u00a0with students,\u00a0faculty, staff,\u00a0alumni, parents,\u00a0and friends\u00a0of the college PHYSICAL\u00a0DEMANDS and\u00a0WORK\u00a0ENVIRONMENT: Mobility:\u00a0walk\u00a0or\u00a0stand\u00a0for\u00a0extended periods\u00a0of\u00a0time Lifting:\u00a0ability\u00a0to\u00a0lift\u00a0and\u00a0carry\u00a050 pounds Dexterity: \u00a0must have\u00a0a\u00a0full\u00a0range\u00a0of\u00a0motion including\u00a0bending,\u00a0stretching,\u00a0lifting,\u00a0and\u00a0kneeling. Be\u00a0available\u00a0for\u00a0scheduled\u00a0shift Overtime\u00a0may\u00a0be\u00a0required Inside\u00a0and\u00a0outside\u00a0of\u00a0buildings,\u00a0spaces\u00a0may\u00a0or\u00a0may\u00a0not\u00a0be\u00a0air\u00a0conditioned Exposure\u00a0to\u00a0potentially hazardous\u00a0chemicals,\u00a0noise,\u00a0dust\u00a0and\u00a0fumes Required\u00a0to\u00a0work\u00a0in\u00a0restricted places\u00a0which\u00a0may\u00a0require stooping,\u00a0bending\u00a0and\u00a0kneeling Buildings\u00a0and\u00a0grounds are\u00a0smoke free Job ID 11710495358 | Posted on May 12, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Related Jobs Lead Custodian Facilities Services Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible SUMMARY:   Ensure campus spaces are safe and clean for students, employees, and guests. Positions available in academic and residential buildings to support student life, academic operations, and ot Boiler Operator & Maintenance Technician Facilities Services Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible SUMMARY   Operate the Luther College Heating Plant in such a manner as to provide a constant uninterrupted supply of steam to the Luther campus. Maintain and validate automation systems for proper a Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"}},